  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-priority question is establishing a simple, well-understood baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: no image processing, no aggregation, no fusion, and a fast linear encoder (PCA). It provides a reference accuracy for the RNA modality with a standard representation. This baseline is essential for later experiments to quantify the marginal value of (a) adding an image modality, (b) switching to learned RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt), (c) moving to multiprofile with aggregation, and (d) different fusion strategies. Starting with the simplest model also minimizes confounding: any future improvement can be attributed to a specific added component rather than to an already-complex starting point. Under a 10-experiment budget, anchoring with the cheapest, most interpretable baseline maximizes the information gained per experiment and reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design axis (which modality and representation carries the most signal)."
}

